; 1389
; 1390    ! QR_ITERATE finds the eigenvalues of the Hessenberg matrix H, EV(1:N),
; 1391    ! working from the bottom: HI is the last row not yet done, and the
; 1392    ! active block is rows and columns L to HI, L just below the last
; 1393    ! negligible subdiagonal element. One QR step on the block, with a shift
; 1394    ! MU: H - MU I = Q R, then R Q + MU I, a similarity again. Q is made of
; 1395    ! plane rotations, each zeroing one subdiagonal element of H - MU I; R Q
; 1396    ! applies them again from the right. The shift is Wilkinson's, the
; 1397    ! eigenvalue of the block's last 2 by 2 nearer its last element, with
; 1398    ! which the last subdiagonal element shrinks quadratically; at the 10th
; 1399    ! and 20th steps without an eigenvalue a different shift breaks any
; 1400    ! cycle. OK is false if an eigenvalue takes more than STEP_LIMIT steps.
; 1401    !
; 1402    ! Only the block is changed: the eigenvalues of a block upper triangular
; 1403    ! matrix are its diagonal blocks', and the rest of H doesn't affect them.
